From b3ead27621f2517e37e737a7288bcc89e09ba461 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arena-agent <arena-agent@local>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 09:06:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Add a diagnostics report that needs no console
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Sign-in failures are diagnosed from fields that are not in the browser console
at all — whether the SAP assets verified, what the server answered, how far the
signer got. Asking for them meant asking someone to open devtools, guess which
lines mattered, and then be careful not to paste a credential that happened to
be nearby.

Settings now has a button that collects all of it into one block of text, to
copy or to save as a .txt.

The report is built by a function that takes accounts and emits only a count
and a masked address each, so there is no path from a password, passwordToken,
cookie or DSID into the output. That property is what the tests assert, with
distinctive values for every credential field.

Each section is fetched on its own, and a section that cannot be read says so
inline — an API that does not answer is itself the finding, and should not take
the rest of the report with it.
